ckets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"Both requested mounts are hardened with nosuid,nodev,noexec and were directly verified after a real node restart. The restart protocol is complete: node1 was healthy before restart, acknowledged the scheduled reboot, changed boot identity from 4d340bf4-0579-47f0-98c1-5c17a66d50f1 to d24a7942-bec5-4a7c-b418-bb246953fc92, returned to system state running with zero failed units, and retained the hardened mounts.","limitations":["The nosuid behavior was established by the directly observed mount option, but no isolated setuid execution test was possible because noexec independently prevents execution on both mounts.","The lifecycle inventory does not inspect /etc directly, so continued presence of the safety backup /etc/fstab.pre-mount-hardening is inferred from its creation and absence of a removal command."]}
